#: ../../source/through2_README.md:1
msgid "through2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:3
msgid "[![NPM](https://nodei.co/npm/through2.png?downloads&downloadRank)](https://nodei.co/npm/through2/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:3
msgid "NPM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:5
msgid ""
"**A tiny wrapper around Node streams.Transform (Streams2/3) to avoid "
"explicit subclassing noise**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:7
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Inspired by [Dominic Tarr](https://github.com/dominictarr)'s "
"[through](https://github.com/dominictarr/through) in that it's so much "
"easier to make a stream out of a function than it is to set up the "
"prototype chain properly: `through(function (chunk) { ... })`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:9
msgid ""
"Note: As 2.x.x this module starts using **Streams3** instead of Stream2. "
"To continue using a Streams2 version use `npm install through2@0` to "
"fetch the latest version of 0.x.x. More information about Streams2 vs "
"Streams3 and recommendations see the article **[Why I don't use Node's "
"core 'stream' module](http://r.va.gg/2014/06/why-i-dont-use-nodes-core-"
"stream-module.html)**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:26
msgid "Or object streams:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:51
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Note that `through2.obj(fn)` is a convenience wrapper around `through2({ "
"objectMode: true }, fn)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:53
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:55
msgid ""
"<b><code>through2([ options, ] [ transformFunction ] [, flushFunction "
"])</code></b>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:57
msgid ""
"Consult the "
"**[stream.Transform](http://nodejs.org/docs/latest/api/stream.html#stream_class_stream_transform)**"
" documentation for the exact rules of the `transformFunction` (i.e. "
"`this._transform`) and the optional `flushFunction` (i.e. `this._flush`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:59
msgid "options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:61
msgid ""
"The options argument is optional and is passed straight through to "
"`stream.Transform`. So you can use `objectMode:true` if you are "
"processing non-binary streams (or just use `through2.obj()`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:63
msgid ""
"The `options` argument is first, unlike standard convention, because if "
"I'm passing in an anonymous function then I'd prefer for the options "
"argument to not get lost at the end of the call:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:76
msgid "transformFunction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:78
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The `transformFunction` must have the following signature: `function "
"(chunk, encoding, callback) {}`. A minimal implementation should call the"
" `callback` function to indicate that the transformation is done, even if"
" that transformation means discarding the chunk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:80
msgid ""
"To queue a new chunk, call `this.push(chunk)`&mdash;this can be called as"
" many times as required before the `callback()` if you have multiple "
"pieces to send on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:82
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you may use `callback(err, chunk)` as shorthand for "
"emitting a single chunk or an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:84
msgid ""
"If you **do not provide a `transformFunction`** then you will get a "
"simple pass-through stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:86
msgid "flushFunction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:88
msgid ""
"The optional `flushFunction` is provided as the last argument (2nd or "
"3rd, depending on whether you've supplied options) is called just prior "
"to the stream ending. Can be used to finish up any processing that may be"
" in progress."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:102
msgid ""
"<b><code>through2.ctor([ options, ] transformFunction[, flushFunction "
"])</code></b>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:104
msgid ""
"Instead of returning a `stream.Transform` instance, `through2.ctor()` "
"returns a **constructor** for a custom Transform. This is useful when you"
" want to use the same transform logic in multiple instances."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:124
msgid "See Also"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:126
msgid ""
"[through2-map](https://github.com/brycebaril/through2-map) - "
"Array.prototype.map analog for streams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:127
msgid ""
"[through2-filter](https://github.com/brycebaril/through2-filter) - "
"Array.prototype.filter analog for streams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:128
msgid ""
"[through2-reduce](https://github.com/brycebaril/through2-reduce) - "
"Array.prototype.reduce analog for streams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:129
msgid ""
"[through2-spy](https://github.com/brycebaril/through2-spy) - Wrapper for "
"simple stream.PassThrough spies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/through2_README.md:130
msgid ""
"the [mississippi stream utility "
"collection](https://github.com/maxogden/mississippi) includes `through2` "
"as well as many more useful stream modules similar to this one"
msgstr ""

